vlib: dispatch pending handoff frames before sleeping

The main loop dequeues inter-thread frames before calling vlib_file_poll(),
but dispatches the resulting pending frames afterwards. Previous-loop vector
counts can be zero at this point. Waiting in epoll then delays work already
dequeued from the handoff queue and can cause NAT handoff congestion even
when the destination worker is not CPU-bound.

Treat pending dispatch frames and newly published frame-queue work as busy.
This does not change the handoff queue capacity or NAT worker selection.

--- a/src/vlib/file.c
+++ b/src/vlib/file.c
@@ -131,6 +131,13 @@
       goto epoll;
     }
 
+  /* Inter-thread frames are dequeued before this call and dispatched after
+   * it. Do not sleep with work already pending, even if the previous loop
+   * processed no vectors. Also notice work published since the dequeue. */
+  if (vec_len (nm->pending_frames) ||
+      __atomic_load_n (&vm->check_frame_queues, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE))
+    goto skip_loops;
+
   /* we are busy, skip some loops before polling again */
   if (vlib_last_vectors_per_main_loop (vm) >= 2)
     goto skip_loops;
